# An owned file's backlinks (docs/extensions.md, "Owners and types, as built"). csv-table,
# installed in the empty home by tests/drive.rs, opens Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv as a table and
# says the view shows that file, so the menu lists who links to it under the table, as it lists
# a note's under the reader: notes, and files other owners read.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
keys /
type eruptions
wait-for ▤ Volcanoes/Eruptions.csv
keys enter j
wait-for CSV table · ⏎ to open it in csv-table
keys enter
wait-for [[Mount St. Helens]]  1980
wait-for Backlinks 1 · b hide
expect ← Start Here
# Another program writes a CSV that links to it: csv-table reads it, and its row is a backlink.
write Volcanoes/Visits.csv Date,Notes\n2026-03-14,Compared the VEIs in [[Eruptions.csv]]\n
wait-for Backlinks 2 · b hide
expect ← Visits.csv
screen
# Tab moves between the table and its backlinks; Enter opens the note at the link.
keys tab
wait-for ← back to the view
keys enter
wait-for a table in a CSV file
expect Backlinks
# Back returns to the table, with its backlinks.
keys ctrl+o
wait-for [[Mount St. Helens]]  1980
expect ← Visits.csv
# Enter on a row of another CSV opens that file in its owner, at the row.
keys tab j enter
wait-for Volcanoes/Visits.csv
expect Compared the VEIs
expect Backlinks none
# b hides the pane under the table, and shows it again.
keys ctrl+o
wait-for [[Mount St. Helens]]  1980
keys b
wait-gone Backlinks 2
keys b
wait-for Backlinks 2 · b hide
keys esc
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys q
exits 0
